<h2>The Creed</h2>
<hr />

<p><em>This is what we hold to be true:</em></p>

<p><strong>We believe</strong> that every person carries a spark of the divine, regardless of the name they give it or whether they give it a name at all.</p>

<p><strong>We believe</strong> that wisdom is not the property of any single book, tradition, or people — it flows freely to those who seek it with honest hearts.</p>

<p><strong>We believe</strong> that the sacred stories are still being written, that prophets still walk among us, and that ordinary people can do extraordinary good.</p>

<p><strong>We believe</strong> in the redemption of the broken, the courage of the afraid, and the power of kindness in a cruel world.</p>

<p><strong>We believe</strong> that doubt is not the enemy of faith — indifference is.</p>

<p><strong>We believe</strong> that true religion is not found in buildings or rituals, but in how we treat the stranger, the widow, the orphan, and the outcast.</p>

<p><strong>We believe</strong> that those who came before us lit torches so we could see — and it is our duty to carry that fire forward.</p>

<p><strong>We believe</strong> in Good Works.</p>

<hr />
<p style="text-align:center;font-style:italic;margin-top:2rem;">
  "Blessed are the wanderers, for they remember that no roof is higher than the sky."
</p>
